# Mercure Hub - Development Environment
# Local copy: `task setup` creates .env.dev from this file; edit the copy.
# Used with: local.Caddyfile (the fork's local-dev compose default)
# WARNING: Do NOT use with the production Caddyfile (admin conflict).

# === JWT Keys (HS256 default) ===
# WARNING: This is a well-known default - never use in production
# Algorithm defaults to HS256 when MERCURE_*_JWT_ALG is empty.
MERCURE_PUBLISHER_JWT_KEY="!ChangeThisMercureHubJWTSecretKey!"
MERCURE_SUBSCRIBER_JWT_KEY="!ChangeThisMercureHubJWTSecretKey!"
MERCURE_PUBLISHER_JWT_ALG=
MERCURE_SUBSCRIBER_JWT_ALG=
#
# === RS256 with PEM key (uncomment to switch) ===
# In compose.yaml, uncomment the `environment:` block: it overrides these
# HS256 values with a multi-line PEM, which .env files cannot hold. The
# Caddyfiles read the key and alg through {env.VAR}, so no Caddyfile edit
# is needed.
# For go:run (no Docker), set PEM inline (shell handles multiline):
#   MERCURE_PUBLISHER_JWT_KEY="$(cat fixtures/jwt/RS256.key.pub)"
#   MERCURE_PUBLISHER_JWT_ALG=RS256
#   MERCURE_SUBSCRIBER_JWT_KEY="$(cat fixtures/jwt/RS256.key.pub)"
#   MERCURE_SUBSCRIBER_JWT_ALG=RS256
#
# === Additional trusted issuer with a JWKS URL ===
# Also trust a second issuer whose keys come from a JWKS endpoint: add an
# `issuer` block to MERCURE_EXTRA_DIRECTIVES below. Each issuer's tokens are
# verified only with the keys bound to it, and its identifier must differ from
# the one local.Caddyfile already declares (MERCURE_TRUSTED_ISSUERS,
# https://localhost by default):
#   issuer https://your-issuer.example.com {
#     publisher {
#       jwks_uri https://gist.githubusercontent.com/lzrf0cuz/e3002e3a7b561f546b5c331e52f729c0/raw/mercure-mock-jwks.json
#     }
#     subscriber {
#       jwks_uri https://gist.githubusercontent.com/lzrf0cuz/e3002e3a7b561f546b5c331e52f729c0/raw/mercure-mock-jwks.json
#     }
#   }
# Note: The hub fetches the JWKS at startup — the URL must be reachable.
# The fixtures/jwt tokens (iss https://localhost) are NOT verified by this
# issuer: a token is checked only against the keys bound to its own `iss`.

# === Server ===
SERVER_NAME="localhost, host.docker.internal"

# Hub identifier: selects the per-hub health endpoint paths and the transport pool key.
MERCURE_HUB_NAME=mercure-dev

# === Mercure Directives ===
# WARNING: DEVELOPMENT ONLY - DO NOT USE IN PRODUCTION
#
# CORS Origins:
# - Header auth (Authorization: Bearer): works with any origin listed
# - Cookie auth (credentials: include): REQUIRES explicit origin, * won't work
#   Add your dev server URL if using cookie auth (e.g., http://localhost:3000)
#
# JWT defaults to HS256 via the `issuer` block in local.Caddyfile.
# To trust a JWKS-backed issuer as well, add another `issuer` block to this
# value (see the JWKS section above for details).
#
# === Transport Selection ===
# The "transport" directive inside MERCURE_EXTRA_DIRECTIVES controls which
# backend the hub uses. Swap by commenting/uncommenting ONE transport block.
# If no transport is specified, the hub defaults to bolt.
#
# Available transports:
#   bolt  — BoltDB, persistent, single-node (default)
#   local — in-memory, no persistence, fastest for dev
#   redis — Redis Streams, persistent, multi-node
MERCURE_EXTRA_DIRECTIVES="
cors_origins https://localhost
publish_origins *
playground
subscriptions
anonymous
transport bolt {
    path ./data/bolt.db
    size 10000
}
heartbeat 15s
write_timeout 300s"
# To switch to local transport, replace the transport block above with:
#   transport local
#
# To run with the redis transport, use `task dev:redis`: it loads
# MERCURE_EXTRA_DIRECTIVES from .env.dev.redis.

# === Caddy Global Options ===
# Dev: verbose logging, and `admin :2019` so the compose port forward
# (127.0.0.1:2019) reaches the admin API from the host. A wildcard admin bind
# disables Caddy's Host check, so other containers on the compose network can
# reach admin; acceptable for a local stack. Production (.env.prod) leaves
# GLOBAL_OPTIONS empty, so the Caddyfile's `admin localhost:2019` applies.
GLOBAL_OPTIONS="debug
servers {
    log_credentials
    trace
}
admin :2019"

# === Caddy Server Directives ===
CADDY_EXTRA_CONFIG=""
CADDY_SERVER_EXTRA_DIRECTIVES="tls internal"
